# Design system

Always use tokens from `src/design-system/`. Never hardcode font family, size, weight, or tracking.

## Type

- Face: **Geist** (sans) and **Geist Mono** (mono) only.
- Use named styles: `type-display`, `type-title`, `type-heading`, `type-body`, `type-body-sm`, `type-label`, `type-caption`, `type-mono`.
- Liquid type via clamp tokens (`--type-*-size`). Do not use `text-sm`, `text-[13px]`, etc.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<p className="text-[13px] font-medium tracking-tight">Label</p>

// ✅ GOOD
<p className="type-label text-[var(--text-muted)]">Label</p>
```

## Breakpoints

Mobile (base) · `tablet` 48rem (768) · `desktop` 80rem (1280) · `desktop-plus` 100rem (1600). Prefer these Tailwind variants over `sm`/`md`/`lg` for layout.

## Tokens

Color, space, radius, shadow, and motion live as CSS variables. Keep semantic aliases (`--bg`, `--text`, …) intact when extending tokens.

## Anti-cliché (tool UI)

- No second hero, welcome subtitle, feature list, or product-name repeat below the top bar.
- No eyebrow labels with wide tracking, marketing chips, star counts, or decorative badges (e.g. “OKLCH”) in chrome.
- No gradient orbs, grain overlays, glassmorphism, gradient text, or purple/glow “AI default” themes.
- No cards. Settings and scales are flat sections, separated by space and a hairline. Do not wrap them in filled panels, nested stages, or repeated radius and shadow.
- Do not animate the page shell: no entrance cascades or floating blobs. UI primitives come from **shadcn/ui** (Radix + Tailwind) restyled with Tintfield tokens. Liquid gooey stays only on press/hover for controls — not as a shared fill bridging shade circles. Color system (Saturated / Fade / Pale) is a quiet Select, not a segmented hero control.
- Prefer `src/components/ui/` shadcn primitives (`Button`, `Select`, `Slider`, `Tooltip`, `DropdownMenu`, `Toaster`). Do not reintroduce SmoothUI. Scale copy formats use a dropdown, not a gooey morph menu.
- Editor layout: wide (`desktop-plus`) is three zones — Adjust panel · ramps · inspector. Below that: full-width ramps with Adjust / Inspector as sheets. Ramp strips are continuous rectangles, not circles.
- Quiet chrome: direct labels, color and ramp are the subject. Keep Geist tokens and the dark minimal palette; do not restyle into a new trendy theme.
- Toasts must not cover the scales column (prefer bottom-left / away from the main ramp view).
